WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.070
Well?

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:04.520
Pardon?

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.030
I switched to wearing glasses.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:07.980
Oh...

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.230
They look nice.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.190
You think so?

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.570
They say that glasses make 
men look 30% more handsome.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.570
So how much progress have you made?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.960
But some girls don't want men 
to cover up their faces.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.200
Kirishima-senpai.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.520
Can you review the new 
school club budget?

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.910
Yep, looks okay.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.590
I trust you know what you're doing.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.050
Right.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.990
That takes care of the club budget.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.490
Next, we need to budget for 
student council expenses.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.820
It seems Hiwako's 
changed quite a bit...

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.030
Don't you have work to do?

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.770
I liked it when she 
was snappy and cool,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.070
but she's even better now 
that she's softened a bit.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:52.820
Oh, you're also cute, Mizuho.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.900
Thank you very much.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.950
So what happened to my proposal?

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.160
What?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.370
For our uniforms.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.080
Come on, now.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.250
As I've said many times, 
we won't be changing our uniforms.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.710
What?!

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.670
Hold on, people!

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:17.100
Are you okay with spending high 
school in these dated uniforms?!

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.100
Girls belong in uniforms that are cuter!

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.880
Maybe if we wait a year...

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.940
I'll be gone then.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.940
Personally, I'm a fan 
of sailor uniforms.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.610
I became student council 
president for nothing, then!

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.360
<i>Why did he choose this school?</i>

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.200
I need to get going.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.580
You're leaving?

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.200
Yes. After all, we're finished.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.910
Then let's go home together, Hiwako!

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.210
There's someone waiting for me.

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.240
Hiwako!

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.680
Bye.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:56.670
Goodbye.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.220
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.520
Don't be. Welcome back.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.100
Thank you.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:27.490
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.290
<b>Humans are Strange</b>

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.540
Thank you very much.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.690
Then we'll continue this tomorrow.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.270
E-Excuse me, Mother...

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.230
What is it?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.350
Well, Father's birthday is soon,

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.700
so I was wondering when 
he would be coming home.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.590
Oh, you're right.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:33.140
He should be back from his 
overseas trip next week.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.180
I see.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.570
Then I'll excuse myself.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:44.440
<i>Next week...</i>

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.880
<i>I hope I can find a 
good present for him.</i>

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.980
You have a new message

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.950
Look what I made!

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.950
Makoto

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.810
Is something wrong?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:39.760
Huh?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.400
Oh. Well, er...

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:47.780
You've been having fun lately 
with your new friends at school,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.240
but you look subdued today.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:52.640
I was wondering if something happened.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.840
You always know everything.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.460
There's something on my mind right now.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.420
If you need someone to talk 
to, I'm always available.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.380
Huh?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.160
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.090
Forgive me for being rude.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.310
You're not.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.000
You don't need to apologize.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.850
Besides, Yoshizumi-san...

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:14.810
Yes?

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:18.040
I feel bad about making
 you drive me around

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.900
when you're my 
father's assistant.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.980
There's no need for you to feel bad!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.070
But the school is close enough 
for me to commute by bike.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.660
Though I've never ridden 
a bicycle before...

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:30.940
Don't worry about it.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.650
Your father has other assistants.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.910
This is part of my job.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.500
Your job...

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.370
Er, I mean...

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.710
I'm sorry.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.540
You have your own reasons 
for being here.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.550
N-No...

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.280
Say, about your offer earlier...

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.930
Would you be willing to listen 
to what's on my mind?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.600
Yes, absolutely.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:56.460
My father's birthday is coming up,

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.180
but I don't know what to give him.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.850
A birthday present for your father?

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:03.310
Perhaps...

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.390
You could go with something 
tried and true like a necktie.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.920
He wears ties every day.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.880
A tie...

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.360
I'm not sure how to pick one.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.240
I don't know my father's tastes.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:19.480
Then I can ask my colleagues 
if they know anything.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:20.670
Thank you.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.760
It must seem strange that I 
don't know my father's tastes.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.250
Your father's busy, so you 
don't get to see him much.

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:27.910
It's perfectly understandable.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.420
Thank you for being so supportive.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:36.010
Do you have any stories to 
tell me about my father?

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.350
You can say bad things 
about him, if you want.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:38.980
That's not...

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:46.000
Say, can I open the window?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:46.860
Go ahead.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:50.650
Let me know if you're going to 
study with your friends again.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.070
Of course, we'll keep it a secret 
from your mother and father.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.280
Our secret?

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:55.510
Yes.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.460
A birthday present?

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.170
Yes, my father's birthday is coming up.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.890
Oh, a present for your dad?

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.230
The last time I gave my dad a 
present was in grade school.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:23.180
I usually ask my dad if 
there's anything he wants,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.280
but he always says that 
anything will do.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:28.190
That doesn't help at all.

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.340
No kidding.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.240
Sorry, Funabashi-san.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.610
We're not much help.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:34.220
It's okay.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.820
I'm thinking about 
giving him a necktie.

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:38.930
A tie?

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:42.640
I asked Yoshizumi-san this morning,

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.210
and he mentioned that my 
father wears ties every day.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.340
Makes sense.

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.310
Your driver is pretty sharp.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.460
Yoshizumi-san isn't my driver.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.280
He's my father's assistant—

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.380
I know, let's ask your driver 
to take us shopping!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.590
As I was saying, 
he's not my driver.

00:08:57.590 --> 00:08:58.790
Look at this.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:01.560
There's a new shopping mall 
that just opened last week.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.150
A shopping mall?

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.100
Oh, I heard about this place.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.770
It's supposed to be huge.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.780
It's not nearby, but if we have someone

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.360
to drive us there and back, 
it's not a problem!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.360
Don't make it sound so simple.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.760
Yoshizumi-san is off tomorrow.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.320
We can take the train...

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.030
We'll be loaded down 
with everything we buy.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.510
Going by car is easier.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.310
Right? Are you coming, Saeki?

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.770
Yep, you bet.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.120
I'm coming along.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.280
See, Funabashi?

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:30.790
There's three of us, 
so we should go by car.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:33.960
We'll help you pick a present, 
so ask him if he can drive us.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:41.760
Fine, but we'll go by train if 
Yoshizumi-san is busy, okay?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.990
Okay, but I'm sure 
he'll agree to take us.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.310
Funabashi Akihiko

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.400
Oh, a necktie.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:55.360
As a politician, the most important 
thing is to present a clean image.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.610
If you're looking for help, 
I believe he has a lot of blue ties.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.820
I see...

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.910
Oh, don't you need to go 
pick up the daughter?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.370
Oh, that's right!

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.830
What? On Saturday?

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.000
Yes, we're looking to go 
shopping somewhere far away.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:15.170
Oh, are you buying a 
present for your father?

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.140
Yes, I feel really bad 
about making you do this.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.050
No, it's no problem at all.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.980
I'm happy to be able to help.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.270
Thank you very much, Yoshizumi-san!

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.560
Thanks for picking me up!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.990
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.870
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:45.850
Check it out!

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:47.330
That's so cute!

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.990
Well? Does it look good?

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:51.140
I think it does.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.150
That doesn't look too bad, Funabashi.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.800
Bikinis are the way to go.

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.460
What do you think about 
this one, Saeki?

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.100
It's a little flashy for me.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.570
This is what you need!

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:11.280
Which one do I pick?

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:13.770
You have a lot of choices.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.350
Hey.

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.820
Isn't this one nice?

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.730
Huh?

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:21.220
U-Um, I'm not sure...

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.580
Whoa! 15,000 yen!

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.400
That's expensive.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.660
I'll put it back.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.040
Oh, Funabashi-san.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:30.310
How about this one?

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:31.990
It's really cute

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:34.540
And it only costs 2,800 yen!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.440
Oh, that's nice.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:37.530
But...

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.180
Which one do you like, then?

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:46.420
Oh, your father's main 
assistant, Kida-san,

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:49.890
said that your father wears 
clean-cut ties for work.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.600
Clean-cut?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.610
And he wears a lot of blue ties.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:58.780
In that case, how would these look?

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:00.780
What do you think?

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.490
Oh, they look nice.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.290
Let's check the price.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.650
8,000 yen?

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:09.390
That's within my budget.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:09.830
Huh?

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.730
But which one do I choose?

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.460
I don't know which one 
will look better.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.170
We have the perfect model here.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.360
Have him try them on.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.750
Wait, you mean me?

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.090
Um, is that okay?

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.300
Uh, yes...

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.910
Excuse me.

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:33.170
Well, it seems like a safe 
choice for a politician.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.350
Yep, what about the other one?

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.640
This one also looks nice.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:43.960
It looks nice, but it seems 
too casual for work.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.920
I think both work.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:49.320
Yep, it comes down to which 
one you want to give him.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.570
I agree.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:53.410
Huh?

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:57.990
Your father buys his own 
ties to use for work,

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:02.040
so you should decide what you 
want to give him as a present.

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:04.720
I'm sure that he wants a present

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:07.300
that his daughter chose for him.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.430
You're right.

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.620
I understand. I'll go with this one.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.080
Thank you for all your help today.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.390
It's no biggie.

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:19.400
Let's grab something to drink.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:20.320
Yep.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:24.280
Yoshizumi-san, do you have enough 
time for us to stick around a bit?

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.230
Absolutely. Take your time.

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.830
I'll be waiting in the car, 
so please call me when you're finished.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.490
Why don't you join us?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.660
I want to thank you for your help today.

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:36.750
Are you sure that's all right?

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:40.710
Look at all the fruits!

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.420
Delicious!

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.870
There seems to be a lot of women here...

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.710
Hey, there's something 
that's been bugging me.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.870
Why did you choose our 
high school, Funabashi?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:56.390
I've never heard of anyone coming 
to our school in a fancy car.

00:13:56.630 --> 00:14:00.080
You're smart enough to get into a 
school for the rich and famous.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:03.400
My mother recommended that
I attend a local high school.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.050
We should be grateful to your mom, then.

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.780
She helped us become friends.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.030
Yes, you're right.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.080
I'm very grateful.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:14.550
This is definitely rare.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.540
It's not easy to find girls 
as sorry as you are.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.450
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:21.380
Now, now.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:25.670
But I have to say that 
you've really changed.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.720
Huh? What do you mean?

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:32.260
Remember how you used 
to snap at everyone?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:34.330
You were really standoffish.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:35.250
Really?

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:36.720
Totally!

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:38.850
You seriously didn't realize it?

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.730
I have to agree that you didn't 
let people approach you.

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.690
That wasn't my intention.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.590
But you've definitely opened up.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.510
Is that so?

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.760
Right? Don't you agree, Driver?

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:53.660
Huh?

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.010
I told you that Yoshizumi-san is my 
driver, not my father's assistant—

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:58.040
Huh?

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:02.420
I mean, he's my father's 
assistant, not my driver!

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.630
Well, either way, don't you agree?

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.050
Y-Yes...

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:17.860
She's running late...

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:25.250
<i>I have to admit that I was 
quite surprised the other day.</i>

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.060
<i>She was having so much 
fun with her friends.</i>

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.330
<i>She certainly feels like 
a different person now.</i>

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:35.580
<i>When I first met her, 
she was almost like a doll.</i>

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.080
Allow me to introduce 
you to my daughter.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.800
My name is Hiwako.
 It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.470
Hiwako, this is Yoshizumi-kun.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.880
He's my youngest assistant 
and just joined us this year.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.110
He'll be taking care of you.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:51.340
Yoshizumi...

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:53.550
<i>Uh, that's not very polite...</i>

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.040
I know that you're busy with work,

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.810
but can you take my daughter 
to and from school?

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:01.100
Also, I'll need you to submit 
a report every day.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:01.760
Of course.

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.060
<i>And now...</i>

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.360
Yoshizumi-san...

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.320
<i>She's become a beautiful girl.</i>

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:12.990
What am I thinking?!

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.610
She's in high school!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.630
Ten years younger than me!

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.950
My boss's daughter!

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.160
What is that guy doing?

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.440
I wonder why she's so late.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:26.000
I'll call her.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:31.810
Yes?

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:32.610
Huh?

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:35.050
Hello, Hiwako's driver.

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:38.260
Aren't you the student 
council president?

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.310
Kirishima Seishiro.

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:41.930
Kirishima-kun?

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.030
So, about Hiwako...

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:45.760
Do you have business with Hiwako-sama?

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.160
Oh, she's not here yet?

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.390
Hmm...

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:50.030
Pardon?

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.000
You can leave, then.

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:54.010
I'll take Hiwako home.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:54.740
Huh?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.140
Don't worry. I'll make sure 
she gets home safely.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.120
Oh, is that Hiwako's phone number?

00:16:59.120 --> 00:16:59.850
Huh?

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:02.650
Excellent. Give it to me.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:04.870
She always refuses to tell 
me her number when I ask.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:04.870
Wait!

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.790
What's the problem?
 This won't cost you anything.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.900
No! No! No!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:13.940
O-Oh, no...

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:15.510
All of my contacts were in here...

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:16.640
What's wrong with you?!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.420
There's no way that I 
could give you her number!

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.260
What is your relationship 
with Hiwako-sama, anyway?!

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:22.420
Come on, you sound like her father.

00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.480
Of course!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.520
I've been asked by her 
parents to take care of her!

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.400
You'll protect her 
from bad boys, right?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:34.000
It's not fair for her to 
be monitored all the time.

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.400
She's in high school now.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:39.390
She should be allowed to spend 
more time with people her age.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.540
Right? You should talk 
to her parents about it.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:45.540
Yoshizumi-san!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.670
Oh, Hiwako!

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:50.000
I'm sorry. One of my friends 
isn't feeling well!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.340
What's wrong?!

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:53.320
Her stomach suddenly started to hurt.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.580
Ow...

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:57.300
The school nurse isn't around! 
Please take us to the hospital!

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:58.180
Huh?

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.800
Ow...

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.220
Are you okay, Kozue-chan?

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.430
U-Uh, Hiwako...

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.100
Oh, Kirishima-senpai.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:05.600
Goodbye!

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:07.770
Let's go! Please!

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:08.810
Y-Yes!

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.820
Shinto Central Hospital

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.730
Sorry about scaring everyone.

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.950
It was just constipation.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.400
I'm glad it wasn't anything serious.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.320
Yes, that's a relief.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:29.420
Someone from my family will 
come pick me up, so I'll be fine.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.420
Thanks a lot.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.590
Saeki-san, I can take you home.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:37.590
Sounds wonderful.

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:42.720
Sorry about dragging 
you around like this.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.380
Oh, it's fine.

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.010
It was an emergency.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.560
I'm more worried about my cell phone...

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:49.430
Is something wrong?

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.210
Er, n-no!

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.480
Oh, it turned on!

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.310
That's great!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.890
Thank you very much.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.040
Oh, do you wanna come up for a bit?

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:14.350
My dad is probably around.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:18.010
Y-You can drop by if you want.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:20.220
You're also welcome, Yoshizumi-san.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.700
Yes, we should visit while we're here.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.260
Er, is it really okay?

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.600
Okay...

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:30.240
Don't worry. We rarely 
see any cars pass by.

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:35.610
I'm home!

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.640
Hold on.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:39.070
Dad!

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:48.210
Now that I think about it,

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:50.390
this is the first time I've met 
someone who lives in a shrine.

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:54.520
Yoshizumi-san, do you know 
how to pay your respects?

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.610
No, I don't know the specific details.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.300
I learned the procedure just recently.

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.330
You go like this...

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:17.150
Since I'm here, I should pray 
for your father's success.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.950
You don't have to do that.

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.720
You should pray for something you want.

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.320
Th-That's true.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:29.700
I know what to do here.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:31.570
I bow twice before clapping my hands.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:32.520
That's right.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:35.240
What's your problem, Gintaro?!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.670
Well, I just thought 
it seemed appropriate.

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:40.560
<i>Something I want...</i>

00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:46.920
<i>Does Hiwako-sama find her 
current lifestyle restrictive?</i>

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:48.850
When you clap your hands together,

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.640
your right hand is supposed 
to be a little lower.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:57.490
After you've made your 
wish, you move it back.

00:20:57.970 --> 00:20:59.020
Did you know that?

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:00.900
I didn't know until they told me.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:03.870
R-Right...

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:21.010
<i>She's my boss's daughter...</i>

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.860
<i>I pray that</i>

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.600
<i>I never fall in love with her!</i>

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.250
Funabashi-san!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.480
Sorry, my dad isn't around.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.980
Really... We should get going, then.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.400
Sorry about this.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:42.690
I wonder where he went.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.570
Why are you sitting in the corner?

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.650
Saeki-san, do you have any 
charms for driving safely?

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:50.870
Yep.

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.340
Here.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:56.370
Please take this.

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:59.210
Th-Thank you very much.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:01.450
Huh? Your face is red, Yoshizumi-san.

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:02.590
Are you okay?

00:22:03.290 --> 00:22:04.580
I might have a cold.

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:07.180
What? Are you feeling all right?

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:09.390
Yes, I'm fine.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.160
We need to get going.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:15.020
I don't get it.

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:16.860
His wish was weird!

00:22:17.150 --> 00:22:19.520
Does it really matter 
what he wished for?

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:21.750
Don't worry about it.

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:24.690
Why can't he fall in love?

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:27.790
This is nothing.

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:30.530
There's a whole world 
of weird out there.

00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:37.990
Humans are strange!

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:19.850
<b>Silver Fox</b>

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:12.360
This is Hiwako.

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:16.100
Normally, a charm is said to 
be effective for one year.

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:19.340
Afterwards, you're supposed to 
return the charm to the shrine.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.300
Next time: "I'm Sorry."

00:24:19.970 --> 00:25:00.000
<b>I'm Sorry</b>

00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:24.840
May fortune be with you.
